sargo: sampler shows kernel stacks and the SDHCI driver state

Early boots froze with one process (seputil, mount_hfs, mount) blocked for
minutes; the sampler only showed its user state (a page fault in dyld).
Each sampled thread now also gets a "k" line: scheduler state, wait event,
block hint and the kernel frame-pointer backtrace (unslid), read from the
thread's saved kernel context as kdp's machine_trace_thread64 does. Each
sample starts with an "SMP sdhci:" line: request/error counts, read mode,
overlay size, requests waiting for the lock, and the request inside the
driver now and for how long. Samples run for an hour (120 x 30 s).

